1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,879
The Orchard Core admin has a theme of its own, separate from the

2
00:00:04,879 --> 00:00:06,265
theme of your site.

3
00:00:06,265 --> 00:00:10,310
In this video, you create an admin theme on top of TheAdmin, change

4
00:00:10,310 --> 00:00:13,580
its branding, restyle its forms, and make it current.

5
00:00:18,180 --> 00:00:20,303
A site has two current themes:

6
00:00:20,303 --> 00:00:24,666
one renders the pages visitors see, and the other renders the admin.

7
00:00:24,666 --> 00:00:29,206
The setup recipes of Orchard Core, such as Blog and Blank, set TheAdmin

8
00:00:29,206 --> 00:00:30,680
as the admin theme.

9
00:00:31,430 --> 00:00:35,170
The Admin attribute marks a request as an admin request.

10
00:00:35,170 --> 00:00:40,840
For those requests, Orchard Core renders with the admin theme instead of the site theme.

11
00:00:41,590 --> 00:00:44,155
Your admin theme does not start from zero.

12
00:00:44,155 --> 00:00:47,895
It names TheAdmin as its base theme, so a template in your theme

13
00:00:47,895 --> 00:00:52,490
replaces the same template of TheAdmin, and every other template stays as it is.

14
00:00:56,690 --> 00:01:01,006
Create the theme project with the theme template, add it to your solution,

15
00:01:01,006 --> 00:01:03,595
and reference it from the web application.

16
00:01:03,595 --> 00:01:06,670
A separate video covers creating a theme in detail.

17
00:01:07,420 --> 00:01:11,889
In the manifest, add the tag admin, and set the base theme to TheAdmin.

18
00:01:11,889 --> 00:01:15,953
The tag lets the Themes page offer your theme as an admin theme.

19
00:01:15,953 --> 00:01:20,480
The base theme makes TheAdmin supply every template you do not override.

20
00:01:21,230 --> 00:01:24,566
The template also adds a Layout file for a site theme.

21
00:01:24,566 --> 00:01:25,455
Delete it.

22
00:01:25,455 --> 00:01:29,736
A Layout in your theme replaces the layout of TheAdmin, which draws the

23
00:01:29,736 --> 00:01:31,960
menu and the top bar of the admin.

24
00:01:36,160 --> 00:01:39,443
To change a template, add a file with the same name to the

25
00:01:39,443 --> 00:01:41,135
Views folder of your theme.

26
00:01:41,135 --> 00:01:44,674
The Razor files of your theme rely on a view imports file, like

27
00:01:44,674 --> 00:01:48,880
the one in TheAdmin, that sets the page class and registers the tag helpers.

28
00:01:49,630 --> 00:01:54,349
The Admin module provides AdminBranding, which renders the brand in the top bar:

29
00:01:54,349 --> 00:01:56,160
the logo and the site name.

30
00:01:56,160 --> 00:02:00,330
Your template keeps only the site name, linked to the admin home page.

31
00:02:01,080 --> 00:02:05,150
The layout renders the branding before the head of the page, so a

32
00:02:05,150 --> 00:02:09,622
stylesheet required here loads on every page that uses the admin layout.

33
00:02:09,622 --> 00:02:12,890
The file lives in the wwwroot folder of your theme.

34
00:02:13,640 --> 00:02:19,322
The depends-on attribute names TheAdminLayout, bootstrap and the-admin, the styles that the layout

35
00:02:19,322 --> 00:02:20,743
loads for the admin.

36
00:02:20,743 --> 00:02:25,660
The browser loads them first and your file after, so your rules can override theirs.

37
00:02:29,860 --> 00:02:32,982
Admin editors do not fix a form layout.

38
00:02:32,982 --> 00:02:36,104
They mark up a field with ocat classes:

39
00:02:36,104 --> 00:02:43,250
ocat-wrapper around the field, ocat-label for its label, and ocat-end for the input and its hint.

40
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:50,846
Fields of limited width, such as dropdowns and numbers, use ocat-limited-wrapper and ocat-limited.

41
00:02:50,846 --> 00:02:55,520
By default, all of these classes stack the label above the input.

42
00:02:56,270 --> 00:03:02,049
Your stylesheet can restyle every editor that uses these classes without touching a Razor view.

43
00:03:02,049 --> 00:03:06,055
This one makes the wrapper a flex row, gives the label a quarter

44
00:03:06,055 --> 00:03:09,660
of the width, aligned to the end, and the input the rest.

45
00:03:13,863 --> 00:03:16,901
Build and run the site, then open Design, Themes.

46
00:03:16,901 --> 00:03:20,878
Your theme appears as a card, after the cards of the current admin

47
00:03:20,878 --> 00:03:23,033
theme and the current site theme.

48
00:03:23,484 --> 00:03:28,667
The card lists the author, the website, the tags and the version from the manifest.

49
00:03:28,667 --> 00:03:33,150
The tags include admin, so Make Current applies this theme to the admin

50
00:03:33,150 --> 00:03:34,664
and not to the site.

51
00:03:35,124 --> 00:03:36,670
Select Make Current.

52
00:03:36,670 --> 00:03:42,734
Orchard Core enables the theme and reports that MyAdminTheme was set as the default Admin theme.

53
00:03:43,186 --> 00:03:44,324
The card reads:

54
00:03:44,324 --> 00:03:49,256
This is the current Admin theme, and every page of the admin renders with your theme.

55
00:03:53,454 --> 00:03:56,117
The top bar shows the branding of your template:

56
00:03:56,117 --> 00:03:57,992
the site name, without the logo.

57
00:03:57,992 --> 00:04:00,704
The rest of the layout still comes from TheAdmin.

58
00:04:01,161 --> 00:04:02,930
Open Settings, General.

59
00:04:02,930 --> 00:04:07,566
Site name, Page title format and Base url each sit beside their field,

60
00:04:07,566 --> 00:04:12,201
because the editors use the ocat classes that your stylesheet changed.

61
00:04:12,654 --> 00:04:15,079
The Settings module did not change.

62
00:04:15,079 --> 00:04:17,445
Only the theme decides the layout.

63
00:04:17,445 --> 00:04:21,704
To go back, make The Admin Theme current again on the Themes page.

64
00:04:25,904 --> 00:04:30,465
Any template of TheAdmin can be replaced the same way, for example Layout,

65
00:04:30,465 --> 00:04:32,518
Breadcrumb, Pager and Message.

66
00:04:32,518 --> 00:04:37,764
A placement file in your theme also changes where parts of the admin pages are placed.

67
00:04:38,514 --> 00:04:42,224
Content fields render their hint with the Hint.Admin template.

68
00:04:42,224 --> 00:04:47,352
A template with that name in your theme replaces it, and reads the text from Model.Hint.

69
00:04:47,352 --> 00:04:49,534
This one renders a tooltip button.

70
00:04:50,284 --> 00:04:53,933
Pages of your own modules use the admin theme when you apply the

71
00:04:53,933 --> 00:04:57,269
Admin attribute to their controller or to a single action.

72
00:04:57,269 --> 00:05:01,804
The Admin module also checks that the user has the Access admin panel permission.

73
00:05:03,804 --> 00:05:05,282
That is an admin theme:

74
00:05:05,282 --> 00:05:08,951
a manifest with the admin tag and TheAdmin as base theme, and only

75
00:05:08,951 --> 00:05:11,499
the templates and styles you want to change.

76
00:05:11,499 --> 00:05:12,824
Thanks for watching.

